APPENDIX A

Redacted DS‑4076 Commodity Jurisdiction Request — Generic Transport Cradle for Launch Vehicle Cylindrical Section

A.1 Filing Preconditions and Procedural Framework

A Commodity Jurisdiction (CJ) determination is the formal procedure described at 22 CFR § 120.4 by which the U.S. Department of State’s Directorate of Defense Trade Controls (DDTC) decides whether an article is covered by the U.S. Munitions List (USML) and therefore subject to the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR). A CJ request is filed on Form DS‑4076. Only a U.S. person or a foreign government may file; a private Moroccan entity cannot self‑file and must engage a U.S. person (counsel or partner) to submit on its behalf. 

DDTC’s instructions state that the submission must include:
- A cover letter on the filer’s letterhead providing an executive summary;
- Complete responses to all blocks on DS‑4076 (no “see attached” replies);
- All supporting documentation at the time of submission;
- A publicly disclosable abstract for posting on the DDTC website. 

Incomplete submissions are Returned Without Action (RWA). The current processing timeline is approximately 65 business days once DDTC confirms receipt and assigns a CJ case number. 

