A.5 Post‑Determination Safeguards

- The CJ determination letter must be retained in the contract file for each delivery.
- Any design modification that adds a flight‑article interface (e.g., hard‑point mating to a specific launch‑vehicle stage) voids the § 120.41(b)(3) basis and requires a new CJ or a DSP‑5 license.
- The Moroccan shop must maintain a “design boundary” log proving that no ITAR‑controlled drawings were received or used.

